-- erwartet: D024
-- **The last writable form of `threads`, and it was green.**
--
-- `D022` refuses every use of a `threads` binder as a PLACE (`t.f`, `t[i]`) or as an INDEX
-- (`T.slots[t]`); `D023` hints where the body never mentions it. Between the two sat one
-- shape that nothing read -- the binder as a plain NUMBER -- and it was measured green
-- against the checker of `6c835eb` on 2026-09-08:
--
--     spec fn alle_klein() -> bool = forall t in threads : t < N;
--         4 items, 0 errors, 0 hints        -- and `pflichten --lean`: total 0
--
-- **And it is the one of the three forms that makes a CLAIM.** `t < N` is true over the
-- empty set, false over the naturals, and *nothing in Gabbro says which set `threads` is*.
-- A statement whose truth value is decided by an undeclared set is not a weak statement,
-- it is an unstated one.
--
-- > **Why a refusal here where `D023` is a hint.** `D023`'s ground is that the vacuous form
-- > is true and useless, and that refusing it would leave `threads` unwritable -- *a
-- > refusal that makes a word of the grammar unwritable is a grammar change wearing a
-- > rule's clothes.* This form is neither true nor false, and refusing it leaves the
-- > vacuous form standing: the word keeps a writable shape, and `D023` goes on saying what
-- > that shape is worth.
--
-- **What `D024` does NOT do.** It does not give `threads` a domain.
-- `messung/GRAMMATIK-VOLLSTAENDIG-2026-09-08.md` §2.3 and `PLAN.md` §9.1 book that as a
-- language change, and `PLAN.md` §15 measures why the obvious surface -- `threads over T`,
-- or a mark at the table -- would be a SYNONYM of `slots of T`: the same index set, the
-- same proposition, byte-identical C, and therefore the very decoration this rule closes.
module gift::threads_ohne_menge {

const N : u32 = 8;

table Faden count N {
    slot {
        zustand : u8,
    }
}

-- The binder is mentioned, so `D023` is silent; it is used as a number and never as a
-- place, so no arm of `D022` can reach it. `D024` is what is left.
spec fn alle_klein() -> bool
    = forall t in threads : t < N;

}
